      "writtenOn": "2026-11-24T19:56:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 58: 🔴 `writeAtomic` uses `std::filesystem::rename(tmp, path)` as if it were a cross-platform atomic replace. On Windows this call fails when `path` already exists, so every subsequent state save fails after the first write. That breaks persisted verified-state/channel-state caching and disables the intended incremental replay path on MSVC builds. Use a replace-capable atomic move on Windows (or an existing project helper that guarantees replace semantics) and keep the same all-or-nothing visibility guarantee.",
      "revId": "625ddb9b252f0b3d629edb5d4c50f2914c21e163",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a9ac98c_b7a0c4dd",
